WEBVTT

00:10.677 --> 00:12.387
You can tell the dead by the look

00:12.887 --> 00:13.847
in their eyes.

00:24.357 --> 00:25.358
That woman…

00:27.694 --> 00:29.237
was definitely dead.

00:29.320 --> 00:30.989
No, we didn't!

00:32.574 --> 00:36.453
I swear we didn't even touch her.
She just died on her own.

00:37.662 --> 00:39.789
Chae-ni! Chae…

00:41.041 --> 00:41.875
Chae-ni?

00:42.959 --> 00:44.377
Chae-ni, where did she go?

00:44.461 --> 00:46.171
-Mr. Son!
-She was right here.

00:46.254 --> 00:47.130
But then,

00:48.089 --> 00:49.215
she vanished.

01:01.770 --> 01:03.980
What a load of nonsense. Jeju Island?

01:04.064 --> 01:05.273
That's what I'm seeing.

01:09.986 --> 01:11.821
Yeah, it's definitely showing Jeju.

01:12.322 --> 01:13.823
Maybe Chae-ni's phone is glitchy.

01:13.907 --> 01:15.658
You're the one who's glitchy.

01:15.742 --> 01:19.204
Don't you know she hasn't once
left Haeseong since she was seven?

01:19.287 --> 01:21.456
Yeah, I know. She's the ghost of Haeseong.

01:21.539 --> 01:22.999
But that's what I'm seeing.

01:23.500 --> 01:24.793
Maybe she really is in Jeju.

01:38.348 --> 01:40.141
That silly bear isn't here either.

01:48.066 --> 01:49.526
She packed her things?

01:55.740 --> 01:57.117
SAVINGS ACCOUNT BANKBOOK

01:59.244 --> 02:01.079
DEAREST GRANDMOTHER

02:08.253 --> 02:10.004
Yes, this is Kim Jeon-bok.

02:10.088 --> 02:13.258
I guess it really was glitchy.
It seems to have been an error.

02:13.341 --> 02:15.468
I tried again, and she's in Haeseong.

02:16.136 --> 02:17.178
In the Haedeul-ri area.

02:24.519 --> 02:28.273
And the victim was Ms. Eun Chae-ni,
the granddaughter of Hearty House?

02:28.898 --> 02:29.774
Yes.

02:30.400 --> 02:31.651
I believe so.

02:32.819 --> 02:35.405
Are you talking about that woman
over there?

02:37.907 --> 02:39.868
Yes, that's right.

02:53.506 --> 02:55.383
Isn't that Chae-ni?

04:06.537 --> 04:10.166
THE WONDERFOOLS

04:11.542 --> 04:16.047
EPISODE 2
SECRETS ARE MEANT TO BE KEPT

04:19.133 --> 04:21.594
You reported the disposal
of a dead body, correct?

04:26.808 --> 04:28.810
Deny it, okay?

04:29.352 --> 04:32.188
Deny it, no matter what.
Deny your butt off.

04:32.897 --> 04:34.774
-That's our only way out.
-Okay.

04:37.652 --> 04:41.030
What dead body? Didn't you see earlier
that Eun Chae-ni is fine?

04:41.114 --> 04:43.908
We were staking the place out
and took a tumble, okay?

04:46.286 --> 04:48.371
Check this stink out for yourself!

04:48.454 --> 04:50.248
I've filed countless complaints,

04:50.331 --> 04:53.835
but the only answer I ever get is,
"No, we can't. There's nothing we can do."

04:53.918 --> 04:56.212
You might as well just play a recording.

05:00.883 --> 05:01.926
What else could we do?

05:02.010 --> 05:05.930
Since the authorities wouldn't step up,
we had to catch the dumper ourselves.

05:07.932 --> 05:08.808
What shall we do?

05:17.025 --> 05:18.568
I guess I was mistaken.

05:20.361 --> 05:22.155
Then we'll log this as a false alarm.

05:22.905 --> 05:25.074
Yes. Please do that.

05:28.369 --> 05:29.370
Okay, you can go.

05:29.454 --> 05:31.289
We were going to. Let's go.

05:32.874 --> 05:33.916
Hey, why would you…

05:46.095 --> 05:47.722
What did I tell you?

05:47.805 --> 05:49.557
I said flat-out denial would work.

05:50.058 --> 05:51.684
You can't call it flat-out denial.

05:51.768 --> 05:53.895
I used sound logic to persuade them.

05:53.978 --> 05:56.022
That's the difference between me and you.

05:56.105 --> 05:58.983
An educated person, an uneducated person.

05:59.067 --> 06:01.402
A good person, a no-good person.

06:02.153 --> 06:05.323
A person whose family is filthy rich,
a person who is dirt poor.

06:06.157 --> 06:07.158
Damn it.

06:08.242 --> 06:10.328
Hey, but are you really okay?

06:10.828 --> 06:13.831
I totally thought you were dead.
Why weren't you breathing?

06:13.915 --> 06:16.084
I thought I was dead too.

06:17.085 --> 06:18.795
I even saw some weird stuff.

06:18.878 --> 06:20.213
What ye doin' o'er there?

06:21.297 --> 06:23.508
Don't loaf around and get outta there.

06:23.591 --> 06:26.761
She kept saying things
that I couldn't understand.

06:26.844 --> 06:30.223
Ain't ye hearin' me?
I said scoot on outta there!

06:30.306 --> 06:33.935
The wind's kickin' up real bad.
At this rate, you ain't gettin' out alone.

06:34.018 --> 06:37.021
Can't ye hear me?
I'm tellin' ya, it's mighty dicey!

06:37.105 --> 06:39.690
What ye doin'? Get outta there already!

06:41.359 --> 06:43.277
Maybe you had a near-death experience.

06:43.361 --> 06:45.113
You know, not actually dying,

06:45.196 --> 06:48.199
but just dipping your toes
into the afterlife.

06:50.118 --> 06:51.869
Maybe you saw a grim reaper!

06:51.953 --> 06:53.287
You think so?

06:54.497 --> 06:56.541
So was I dead or not?

06:57.625 --> 06:58.793
Maybe I half-died.

07:00.044 --> 07:02.130
Like a half-dried squid or something?

07:02.964 --> 07:05.383
Does your grandma know
the shape you're in?

07:06.217 --> 07:07.927
Of course she doesn't.

07:08.010 --> 07:09.804
If she did, she'd lose it.

07:09.887 --> 07:11.597
Don't you know what she's like?

07:11.681 --> 07:14.225
The big cheese of Myeong-dong,
King Jeon-bok.

07:15.518 --> 07:16.602
If she finds out…

07:16.686 --> 07:17.854
If she finds out?

07:18.187 --> 07:19.355
EUN CHAE-NI'S

07:19.439 --> 07:20.690
KIDNAPPERS

07:26.112 --> 07:28.197
We're truly sorry, ma'am.

07:31.617 --> 07:32.827
Go on and bury them.

07:32.910 --> 07:34.287
Yes, ma'am!

07:34.370 --> 07:36.456
Please don't do that!

07:39.750 --> 07:40.710
Hold it!

07:42.587 --> 07:44.464
Why are you over there, not here with us?

07:46.466 --> 07:49.135
What was that word
I told you to memorize again?

07:49.218 --> 07:52.054
How diplomats
get away with crimes overseas.

07:52.138 --> 07:55.099
-Immunity.
-That's it. Granddaughter immunity.

07:56.100 --> 07:58.269
Is there no
granddaughter's friend immunity?

07:58.352 --> 07:59.395
What do I do now?

07:59.479 --> 08:01.439
Hey, Mr. Son, what should we do?

08:01.522 --> 08:04.525
Why did you rope us into this?
You could've just stolen the money.

08:04.609 --> 08:07.236
It's okay.
We'll make sure we don't get caught.

08:07.320 --> 08:08.654
Flat-out denial always works.

08:08.738 --> 08:10.781
You think denial will cut it?

08:10.865 --> 08:12.450
Is that the best you can do?

08:12.533 --> 08:14.368
Who said you'll just deny it?

08:15.536 --> 08:17.622
Deny with passion, with all you've got.

08:19.874 --> 08:22.919
Would that actually work?
Then we'd be in the clear, right?

08:23.002 --> 08:25.463
Of course. Nothing beats flat-out denial.

08:29.509 --> 08:30.468
Did you really

08:30.551 --> 08:34.055
think this plan through carefully?

08:34.555 --> 08:36.432
How would you have gotten the 50 million?

08:36.516 --> 08:38.017
Wired to my account, of course.

08:38.518 --> 08:40.394
Borrowed accounts are illegal, you know.

08:45.024 --> 08:48.528
I had no clue because I'd never
talked to you long enough.

08:49.070 --> 08:52.740
That you were a girl
with such an empty head.

08:52.823 --> 08:55.076
To think I trusted bozos like you

08:55.618 --> 08:58.788
and co-conspired to get 50 million won…

08:58.871 --> 09:00.331
-Want some?
-What are they?

09:02.416 --> 09:03.709
-These are good.
-Right?

09:03.793 --> 09:05.461
Hey, I'm talking to you!

09:15.638 --> 09:18.307
This is my fault. It's all my fault.

09:18.391 --> 09:22.728
I, a Homo sapiens who conspired
with Neanderthals, am to blame.

09:24.021 --> 09:24.855
If I ever

09:25.356 --> 09:28.985
get involved in another ridiculous
fake kidnapping of Eun Chae-ni

09:29.068 --> 09:31.988
or another half-dried squid
near-death experience,

09:32.071 --> 09:33.823
you can consider me…

09:33.906 --> 09:34.865
Screwed.

09:41.664 --> 09:42.707
She heard.

09:43.291 --> 09:44.125
Everything.

10:00.725 --> 10:02.059
Run!

10:14.989 --> 10:18.242
You know the crimes you are guilty of!

10:20.745 --> 10:23.164
Punish him mercilessly!

10:29.795 --> 10:33.215
I am innocent. Treason, of all crimes?

10:33.299 --> 10:35.676
This is preposterous.

10:36.385 --> 10:38.387
I truly am innocent.

10:39.055 --> 10:43.768
I swear to the heavens above
that I have not one speck of shame.

10:43.851 --> 10:44.977
How dare you!

10:45.936 --> 10:49.690
Twist his legs until he confesses!

10:54.153 --> 10:57.031
I have done no wrong!

11:10.836 --> 11:12.713
Is this thing really glitching?

11:15.758 --> 11:16.676
Come out.

11:19.178 --> 11:21.055
Come here
before I get people to drag you out!

11:25.685 --> 11:28.479
Ms. Kim…

11:30.398 --> 11:32.024
Could you please move…

11:35.528 --> 11:37.321
That… No, it's okay.

11:37.405 --> 11:38.739
Thank you.

11:39.949 --> 11:44.245
Just moving one of your legs
is more than enough for me to get out.

11:44.328 --> 11:45.413
Like this.

11:55.047 --> 11:57.717
-You must be furious.
-I tried to talk her out of it.

11:57.800 --> 12:01.053
-But it was all Chae-ni's plan.
-I said, "Think about your grandma."

12:01.137 --> 12:03.889
-She said we'd get five million each--
-I really tried--

12:05.850 --> 12:08.811
In other words, the three of you

12:09.645 --> 12:12.106
staged a kidnapping for money?

12:12.189 --> 12:16.694
-I wouldn't quite put it like that.
-Mr. Son here wouldn't fix my roof.

12:16.777 --> 12:19.321
-Chae-ni planned all of this--
-I just wanted my roof--

12:21.741 --> 12:23.159
Where's your mastermind, Eunie?

12:23.242 --> 12:26.829
That's exactly it!
Eun Chae-ni is the mastermind, Ms. Kim.

12:29.915 --> 12:30.875
Eunie.

12:31.375 --> 12:35.379
Your accomplices have already betrayed you
without hesitation. Get out here.

12:39.133 --> 12:42.762
Why, you always make
things worse for yourself!

12:43.345 --> 12:44.555
Get out here!

12:48.142 --> 12:49.059
What?

12:50.728 --> 12:52.855
I definitely saw her climb in here.

12:57.067 --> 12:58.486
Where were you hiding?

12:59.445 --> 13:00.279
Grandma.

13:02.323 --> 13:03.240
Can you see me?

13:03.324 --> 13:05.826
What newfangled nonsense is this?

13:05.910 --> 13:08.454
Did you think I wouldn't be able
to see you? Get out now!

13:10.289 --> 13:11.290
Deary me.

13:11.373 --> 13:12.792
What do I do, Grandma?

13:14.043 --> 13:16.420
Something must be really wrong with me.

13:17.004 --> 13:20.299
I keep seeing things. What do I do?

13:20.382 --> 13:21.425
How?

13:21.926 --> 13:25.137
What feels wrong? How?
Should I call the hospital director?

13:25.221 --> 13:27.556
-I don't know.
-Are you running a fever?

13:28.098 --> 13:29.141
-Oh dear.
-I just…

13:31.101 --> 13:34.605
Would you look at that?
She's using her granddaughter immunity.

13:36.816 --> 13:37.858
Tell me what happened.

13:37.942 --> 13:40.653
-Just now, I was in some weird…
-Yes, what is it?

13:40.736 --> 13:42.863
-Yes?
-Grandma!

13:42.947 --> 13:45.407
Breathe. Just breathe. And sit down.

13:45.491 --> 13:48.452
Sit right here and take a deep breath.

13:48.953 --> 13:50.746
Just take a breath.

13:52.748 --> 13:53.666
He's annoying.

13:53.749 --> 13:55.876
He's annoying? That's no good.

13:55.960 --> 13:57.628
Hey, you're annoying her!

14:00.548 --> 14:02.258
You're looking for someone?

14:03.551 --> 14:04.426
Who?

14:05.052 --> 14:06.512
The Child of Eternity?

14:08.889 --> 14:09.974
I don't know.

14:11.809 --> 14:15.938
There were some children
who survived the fire back then.

14:17.857 --> 14:21.402
But I'm not sure about
this Child of Eternity you speak of.

14:24.905 --> 14:31.078
Oh, but I do remember
one other child very clearly.

14:32.204 --> 14:33.789
Number 3972.

14:35.499 --> 14:37.543
Because I saved him

14:38.711 --> 14:40.713
from the fire that day.

14:46.927 --> 14:49.096
Sir!

14:49.179 --> 14:51.140
Please open this door!

14:51.640 --> 14:53.517
Please open this door!

14:58.063 --> 14:59.398
Number 3972?

14:59.481 --> 15:01.775
You saved that child?

15:01.859 --> 15:04.737
Yes, I sure did.

15:06.739 --> 15:08.157
And that child

15:09.366 --> 15:11.285
has returned to Haeseong.

15:13.621 --> 15:15.497
He's grown into a fine young man.

15:15.581 --> 15:18.042
He didn't seem to recognize me,

15:18.542 --> 15:21.378
but I recognized him right away.

15:21.879 --> 15:23.380
Number 3972.

15:24.965 --> 15:26.717
I'm certain it's him.

15:28.093 --> 15:29.219
I see.

15:29.720 --> 15:31.430
Thank you for telling me.

15:32.306 --> 15:34.099
Here, eat up before it gets cold.

15:56.080 --> 15:59.208
I don't know how many years it's been

15:59.291 --> 16:01.585
since I sat across from you like this…

16:03.462 --> 16:05.631
and ate a hot meal.

16:11.261 --> 16:13.055
After you died,

16:14.431 --> 16:17.643
I was sure a day like this
would never come again.

16:20.604 --> 16:23.482
I'm so glad you're here.

16:36.453 --> 16:38.998
Did you hear that? Number 3972.

16:45.129 --> 16:46.088
Honey.

16:48.882 --> 16:50.175
Honey!

16:50.759 --> 16:53.887
Where… where am I?

16:54.638 --> 16:55.639
Honey?

17:04.898 --> 17:06.150
NUMBER 3972
ABILITY: TELEKINESIS

17:06.233 --> 17:07.943
What is all this?

18:18.931 --> 18:21.183
Don't you have a family?

18:23.602 --> 18:24.603
I don't know.

18:25.771 --> 18:27.481
I can't remember.

18:28.357 --> 18:29.775
Not even your mom's face?

18:30.442 --> 18:31.485
Or your dad's?

19:36.049 --> 19:36.967
Don't worry.

19:37.467 --> 19:38.760
I can't die.

19:39.553 --> 19:41.680
You can't die?

19:51.940 --> 19:55.235
Focus and try again. You can do it.

20:39.780 --> 20:40.906
How did he do that?

20:42.157 --> 20:43.659
That's awesome.

21:07.140 --> 21:08.976
Stop!

21:42.009 --> 21:43.927
You're still doing this, City Hall guy?

21:44.011 --> 21:46.305
I asked you
to please keep it down at night!

21:46.805 --> 21:48.515
You're really trying my patience.

21:49.016 --> 21:50.934
Knock it off or move out already!

21:53.478 --> 21:55.772
I can't die.

21:59.276 --> 22:00.819
But that kid was definitely

22:01.695 --> 22:02.988
a boy.

22:52.913 --> 22:53.830
What…

22:54.998 --> 22:55.832
Huh?

22:57.584 --> 22:58.502
How?

23:00.879 --> 23:02.464
Why, what is it?

23:02.547 --> 23:04.883
Is something wrong? Is it very serious?

23:04.966 --> 23:06.426
Well, it's…

23:07.886 --> 23:11.139
I'm ready for anything, so just tell me.

23:11.223 --> 23:12.307
Spit it out!

23:13.517 --> 23:14.726
Well,

23:15.310 --> 23:16.144
it's very…

23:17.646 --> 23:20.857
I don't quite understand
how this has happened either,

23:20.941 --> 23:22.734
but the test results are…

23:22.818 --> 23:24.444
Everything here

23:25.946 --> 23:26.822
looks normal.

23:27.989 --> 23:28.824
Come again?

23:28.907 --> 23:32.119
If you look at the graphs here,

23:32.202 --> 23:35.539
you can see they're all very stable
with no major fluctuations.

23:35.622 --> 23:37.290
This is from last time. This is now.

23:37.916 --> 23:40.252
I checked the ultrasound results, too,

23:40.335 --> 23:42.045
and her kidneys look clean.

23:42.129 --> 23:45.132
Even the valvular inflammation
I saw last time is completely gone.

23:45.215 --> 23:49.010
And this is the X-ray we just took.
That one's from last time.

23:49.094 --> 23:50.929
Her lungs have cleared up too.

23:51.012 --> 23:52.889
Last time, her heart was this big,

23:53.473 --> 23:54.516
but now,

23:55.267 --> 23:57.727
it's back to a completely normal size.

23:57.811 --> 23:59.271
So, you're saying…

24:01.440 --> 24:03.942
To get this straight,

24:05.277 --> 24:06.695
you seem to be saying

24:07.195 --> 24:08.947
that everything has improved.

24:09.448 --> 24:10.991
Would that be right?

24:11.074 --> 24:13.452
No, ma'am, it's not just an improvement.

24:15.245 --> 24:16.371
She's in

24:16.955 --> 24:18.206
perfect health.

24:19.624 --> 24:20.459
How?

24:20.542 --> 24:23.378
Exactly! I've never seen
anything like this before.

24:23.462 --> 24:26.882
Of course, once in a blue moon,
things like this do happen,

24:26.965 --> 24:28.758
and there's no telling why.

24:28.842 --> 24:31.386
We usually call them miracles.

24:33.263 --> 24:34.806
I think, ma'am, that Chae-ni

24:35.515 --> 24:37.225
has been blessed with a miracle.

24:40.187 --> 24:41.104
A miracle?

24:41.730 --> 24:43.815
This child is a miracle child.

25:31.071 --> 25:35.033
CHOI YEONG-JUN

25:46.086 --> 25:49.005
This is Choi Yeong-jun.
Please leave a message.

25:49.506 --> 25:51.258
Hello, Director Choi. It's me.

25:52.133 --> 25:53.927
King Jeon-bok of Myeong-dong.

25:54.469 --> 25:56.263
Call me when you get this.

26:06.106 --> 26:09.109
CHURCH OF ETERNAL SALVATION

26:09.192 --> 26:11.403
APOCALYPSE ON DECEMBER 31ST

26:11.486 --> 26:14.948
RECEIVE SALVATION
AND BE GRANTED ETERNAL LIFE

26:22.581 --> 26:25.458
APOCALYPSE
SALVATION

26:33.466 --> 26:35.051
What do we do now, Mr. Son?

26:35.552 --> 26:38.179
How will we ever face Ms. Kim now?

26:38.680 --> 26:39.806
You tell me.

26:40.307 --> 26:43.643
I refused, but you two insisted on
roping me into this. So tell me.

26:44.352 --> 26:45.437
Mr. Son.

26:45.937 --> 26:49.274
If you hadn't assumed Chae-ni was dead,
we wouldn't be in this mess.

26:49.941 --> 26:50.775
Assumed?

26:51.401 --> 26:52.235
Listen.

26:52.861 --> 26:54.654
She was definitely dead.

26:54.738 --> 26:56.281
She didn't have a pulse.

26:56.364 --> 26:59.075
How could a dead person come back to life?

26:59.159 --> 27:02.287
You went as far as to dispose of
a perfectly healthy person in the hills.

27:02.370 --> 27:04.623
Quiet. Temporarily laid to rest,
not disposed of.

27:05.707 --> 27:07.292
Besides, did I act alone?

27:07.375 --> 27:08.835
You're even worse than I am.

27:08.918 --> 27:12.339
How could you, her friend,
dump her body in a garbage pit?

27:15.884 --> 27:16.926
Mr. Son!

27:17.427 --> 27:20.096
That's why I said we shouldn't do it.

27:20.180 --> 27:23.475
Of course, there it is!
There go the waterworks again.

27:23.558 --> 27:27.812
You look like a thug,
but you cry and sulk at the drop of a hat!

27:27.896 --> 27:30.732
Do you know how ghastly
your crying face is?

27:31.691 --> 27:34.736
Don't make fun of people's looks.
You shouldn't do that.

27:34.819 --> 27:37.322
Do you think I'm making fun of your looks?

27:37.405 --> 27:38.657
I'm not.

27:39.574 --> 27:41.409
Wait, you weren't? Really?

27:41.493 --> 27:43.328
Of course not.

27:43.411 --> 27:47.040
I was going for a double whammy
by making fun of your looks and sulkiness.

27:47.123 --> 27:48.500
Get a clue, Sappy Sap.

27:48.583 --> 27:50.794
With your runny nose.
God, you drive me nuts.

28:15.276 --> 28:17.362
I told you not to drink from the bottle.

28:22.784 --> 28:23.743
By the way,

28:24.244 --> 28:26.830
any news about the illegal dumping
in the hills?

28:26.913 --> 28:27.747
What?

28:28.248 --> 28:29.332
Right, that.

28:29.416 --> 28:32.252
I actually went earlier
and gave them a good talking-to.

28:32.335 --> 28:34.003
Any time now. Don't worry.

28:35.088 --> 28:36.047
And your mother?

28:37.257 --> 28:38.091
What?

28:38.174 --> 28:40.009
Did you make it clear to her

28:40.093 --> 28:43.346
that we're not sending her to Hawaii
but the Hawaii Resort in Bugok?

28:45.432 --> 28:48.977
Yeah, that. Well, you know…

28:49.978 --> 28:52.564
She knows our situation, after all.

28:53.398 --> 28:55.316
She didn't seem too disappointed.

29:14.419 --> 29:16.588
What are you even doing?

29:17.130 --> 29:19.048
I just have some things to think about.

29:19.132 --> 29:20.467
Do you have to do it there?

29:20.550 --> 29:22.802
Yeah, I have to do it here.

29:23.928 --> 29:25.180
Well, I'm going to bed.

29:25.263 --> 29:27.015
Okay, good night, Ms. Moon Mi-hui.

29:45.325 --> 29:49.287
Here comes my daughter, Cheong,
just as I was opening the fridge door.

29:51.664 --> 29:53.124
Want some ice to cool down?

29:57.837 --> 29:58.671
So that's a no?

30:03.718 --> 30:05.762
Are you the problem or am I?

30:05.845 --> 30:09.557
If you are, I can call for a repair,
but who do I call if I'm the problem?

30:27.659 --> 30:29.118
How can this…

30:32.747 --> 30:33.623
How…

31:29.929 --> 31:31.639
Who exactly were your accomplices?

31:37.812 --> 31:38.855
I acted alone.

31:38.938 --> 31:40.857
Ro-bin and Sonie from the flower shop.

31:40.940 --> 31:42.901
I know those two idiots were involved.

31:43.651 --> 31:44.903
Was there anyone else?

31:45.612 --> 31:48.489
I told you. The three of us acted alone.

31:50.617 --> 31:52.368
Do you not know what "alone" means?

31:53.870 --> 31:56.497
I sure do. I know very well.

31:58.458 --> 32:00.543
The soup's getting cold. Eat.

32:03.630 --> 32:07.258
How did you even plan to travel
without a passport?

32:15.600 --> 32:18.186
What did the doctor say?

32:19.270 --> 32:22.482
Did he give you some bad news?

32:23.691 --> 32:25.234
While you were growing up,

32:25.818 --> 32:27.904
there wasn't a day that I didn't pray

32:29.113 --> 32:31.199
nor a single day I had peace of mind.

32:31.866 --> 32:35.328
If I couldn't reach you for just a moment,
my heart would sink.

32:35.411 --> 32:38.665
Every time I took you to the hospital,
my blood ran cold.

32:40.667 --> 32:42.335
That's how scared I've been

32:43.252 --> 32:44.253
for the past 20 years.

32:47.632 --> 32:48.758
But

32:50.301 --> 32:52.261
no matter how scared I was…

32:54.222 --> 32:55.640
I doubt I was as scared as you.

33:04.273 --> 33:05.400
I'm sorry, Grandma.

33:06.859 --> 33:08.486
What are you sorry for?

33:08.569 --> 33:11.698
You've made me
the happiest I've been in 27 years.

33:13.574 --> 33:16.035
The test results were excellent.

33:16.703 --> 33:18.621
He said everything's normal.

33:19.288 --> 33:21.290
I never thought I'd see this day.

33:21.374 --> 33:23.376
You're as clean as a whistle.

33:23.459 --> 33:26.462
The size, shape, and condition
of your heart are all perfect.

33:26.546 --> 33:27.922
Why, that doctor

33:28.423 --> 33:31.467
made a huge fuss, calling it a miracle.

33:34.512 --> 33:35.763
So,

33:36.723 --> 33:37.724
from now on,

33:38.808 --> 33:41.102
live your life to the fullest, okay?

33:42.145 --> 33:45.106
But don't let your guard down
and get regular checkups.

33:45.189 --> 33:46.190
What was it, again?

33:46.691 --> 33:50.069
Go see the northern lights or whatever
and that huge-headed rock.

33:50.737 --> 33:53.906
And what was it?
Go see the Iguana Falls or whatever.

33:53.990 --> 33:55.533
And go explore Africa.

33:56.409 --> 33:57.618
You should do it all.

33:59.287 --> 34:00.329
So,

34:00.413 --> 34:01.831
from now on,

34:02.707 --> 34:04.417
live life to the fullest, okay?

34:05.877 --> 34:07.378
Make the darn most of it,

34:09.005 --> 34:10.423
and pay for your own trips.

34:19.557 --> 34:22.560
How will I ever earn enough
peeling onions?

34:38.117 --> 34:38.993
Grandma!

34:42.038 --> 34:43.289
Before that…

34:46.459 --> 34:47.293
REWARD GRAPES

34:47.376 --> 34:48.628
…you need to fill this up.

34:49.879 --> 34:50.838
Until then,

34:51.339 --> 34:54.383
be good, stay healthy, and speak politely.

34:54.467 --> 34:57.720
And don't spit on other people's houses.
Then I'll give these to you.

34:59.472 --> 35:03.309
Come on, Grandma. I'm not seven.

35:03.392 --> 35:05.144
I'm 27 years old.

35:05.228 --> 35:07.188
If you don't like it, best get peeling.

35:07.271 --> 35:08.606
Oh no.

35:12.193 --> 35:13.236
All right.

35:14.862 --> 35:16.906
First, eat all your food.

35:35.091 --> 35:38.594
Yes, this is Kim Jeon-bok of Hearty House.

35:47.520 --> 35:49.272
It's been a while, Director Choi.

36:08.875 --> 36:10.168
"Great job."

36:18.593 --> 36:20.553
No more purple lips.

36:22.513 --> 36:24.015
No more dull skin.

36:26.017 --> 36:27.476
No more tinnitus.

36:29.061 --> 36:30.104
And no more bruises.

36:33.691 --> 36:35.610
Even my heart's beating fine.

36:37.570 --> 36:40.907
There's been a definite improvement
since my near-death experience.

36:42.533 --> 36:44.368
So why do I keep seeing things?

36:44.452 --> 36:47.246
What ye doin'? Get outta there already!

36:48.915 --> 36:50.082
But that place

36:51.083 --> 36:52.668
wasn't even a tunnel.

37:00.384 --> 37:01.677
Could it be time…

37:02.178 --> 37:04.513
I can't even bring myself
to say "time travel."

37:10.770 --> 37:11.938
That's right.

37:12.438 --> 37:15.775
My brain must have been
deprived of oxygen for a long time.

37:16.275 --> 37:18.069
That's for certain.

37:24.533 --> 37:26.619
There's no doubt they were hallucinations.

37:27.119 --> 37:28.037
Wait a minute.

37:28.621 --> 37:30.873
Then in exchange for a working heart…

37:31.707 --> 37:34.210
7 times 5 is 35, 7 times 6 is 42,
7 times 7 is 49…

37:34.293 --> 37:37.129
-7 times 8 is…
-Don't touch your eyes, idiot!

37:41.050 --> 37:44.428
Did I lose my brain
in exchange for a working heart?

37:46.639 --> 37:49.016
-This can't be.
-Chae-ni, you have a guest outside.

37:49.100 --> 37:50.309
It's a guy.

37:50.393 --> 37:52.061
He's a looker.

37:53.062 --> 37:54.730
Don't touch your eyes. It stings.

37:55.648 --> 37:56.482
Don't move.

38:00.987 --> 38:02.113
Why are you here?

38:02.613 --> 38:03.948
What do you want from me?

38:04.740 --> 38:05.783
Here to pay up?

38:08.035 --> 38:09.245
How many times have you died?

38:14.375 --> 38:15.209
Me?

38:15.293 --> 38:17.003
Was that the first time?

38:17.712 --> 38:19.046
Or have you died before?

38:22.216 --> 38:24.468
Is he saying he wants to die?

38:24.552 --> 38:26.554
No. That's him.

38:26.637 --> 38:28.556
The guy who reported us
for dumping a body.

38:28.639 --> 38:30.975
When you had
that near-death experience yesterday.

38:31.058 --> 38:32.727
I see.

38:33.227 --> 38:36.981
First, you wreck my suitcase,
then you make a big fuss over nothing?

38:37.064 --> 38:40.568
I reported it for your sake.
So they could at least find your body.

38:40.651 --> 38:42.111
My body?

38:42.194 --> 38:44.280
I'm standing right here, alive and well!

38:44.363 --> 38:46.490
-You were definitely dead.
-No, I wasn't!

38:46.574 --> 38:49.327
You're making me sound like
some kind of freak.

38:49.952 --> 38:50.828
So what happened?

38:54.790 --> 38:55.833
It's a secret.

38:58.336 --> 39:00.254
She's definitely hiding something.

39:00.838 --> 39:02.131
So you can't tell me?

39:03.758 --> 39:05.676
It's a secret because I can't tell you.

39:05.760 --> 39:08.179
It wouldn't be a secret
if I could tell you, would it?

39:15.102 --> 39:16.228
Then, have you ever…

39:24.028 --> 39:25.196
heard of Wunderkinder?

39:26.989 --> 39:28.115
What's this

39:28.657 --> 39:31.369
Boon… the King Duck?

39:31.869 --> 39:33.037
I don't even like duck.

39:33.913 --> 39:35.623
Is it a new duck joint or something?

39:35.706 --> 39:39.752
Why do you keep bothering us?
We told you that nothing happened.

39:39.835 --> 39:41.545
See? Nothing happened.

39:45.466 --> 39:46.634
Well, okay, then.

39:47.176 --> 39:48.344
If you say so.

39:58.396 --> 40:00.981
What was that?
We've got ourselves a nutjob, right?

40:01.065 --> 40:03.359
What if he finds out about the kidnapping?

40:03.442 --> 40:04.819
It was my idea anyway.

40:05.736 --> 40:09.407
But Mr. Son said we could be in trouble
if the police find out!

40:09.490 --> 40:11.283
They'd have no evidence anyway.

40:13.828 --> 40:16.831
You grabbed my suitcase
and camcorder, didn't you?

40:17.706 --> 40:20.501
No. They're probably still
in the abandoned greenhouse.

40:21.877 --> 40:23.295
You didn't delete the footage?

40:24.046 --> 40:25.297
No.

40:25.381 --> 40:27.508
You died,
and we were so freaked out that--

40:28.801 --> 40:30.428
Oh, for God's sake!

40:30.511 --> 40:32.888
You're peeling my share
of the onions for today.

40:32.972 --> 40:35.891
And tomorrow and the day after that
and after that! All yours!

40:44.733 --> 40:47.194
Mr. Son? It's Ro-bin.

40:48.154 --> 40:49.572
Okay, goober. Talk later.

40:53.576 --> 40:56.203
I knew I shouldn't have gotten mixed up
with those bozos.

40:57.538 --> 40:59.373
Everything's going sideways.

41:03.419 --> 41:06.672
Please, Rala.
Why are you giving me a hard time too?

41:11.260 --> 41:12.720
That's it, you beauty.

41:34.950 --> 41:38.829
Okay, your turn for lunch.
Today's menu is jjajangbap. Go eat.

41:38.913 --> 41:41.499
Un-jeong, you should also…
You're already gone.

41:41.582 --> 41:45.294
He went alone again, that brat.

41:45.377 --> 41:46.504
Oh boy.

41:53.010 --> 41:55.846
There's only one way to find out for sure
if she possesses

41:56.347 --> 41:57.890
the ability to resurrect.

41:59.225 --> 42:01.185
Make her need to revive herself.

42:46.897 --> 42:47.773
Extra crispy.

43:27.730 --> 43:29.148
But what if

43:29.815 --> 43:30.649
I'm wrong?

43:53.756 --> 43:54.673
Excuse me.

44:09.396 --> 44:14.652
HAEWON FLOWERS

44:35.673 --> 44:38.425
Is it broken or something?
Why isn't it working?

44:39.051 --> 44:42.179
It'll be worth more if it's working.

44:43.931 --> 44:44.848
What the…

44:48.185 --> 44:50.479
Chae-ni. Chae-ni?

44:50.562 --> 44:51.730
What's wrong with her?

44:53.899 --> 44:54.983
Delete that.

44:55.067 --> 44:56.485
-What's this?
-What? Why?

45:01.740 --> 45:03.867
What is it?

45:04.451 --> 45:06.203
What's wrong with Chae-ni?

45:06.787 --> 45:09.081
And what's wrong with you?

45:10.124 --> 45:11.083
Chae-ni

45:12.459 --> 45:13.585
is dead.

45:17.589 --> 45:18.549
Chae-ni

45:19.591 --> 45:21.218
is dead.

45:27.015 --> 45:28.392
I'll buy this from you.

45:31.311 --> 45:33.856
Where the heck did they leave them?

45:35.065 --> 45:37.860
Did they really leave them here?

45:42.114 --> 45:43.365
This is it?

45:44.116 --> 45:46.618
Where's the other stuff?

45:58.422 --> 45:59.339
Damn it.

45:59.423 --> 46:03.135
That bumbling idiot.
How could he leave that stuff there?

46:47.596 --> 46:49.556
What's going on? What's happening?

47:05.364 --> 47:07.032
Where are you right now?

47:07.741 --> 47:08.575
What?

47:08.659 --> 47:11.328
Where else would I be?
I'm making a delivery, of course.

47:13.664 --> 47:16.834
Well, if the flowers
you're supposed to deliver are right here,

47:17.334 --> 47:18.794
what exactly are you delivering?

47:18.877 --> 47:19.711
What?

47:20.212 --> 47:21.046
What the…

47:21.129 --> 47:23.340
What do you mean, what?
I should be asking you!

47:23.423 --> 47:25.467
What exactly are you doing?

47:25.968 --> 47:27.636
-What…
-What?

47:27.719 --> 47:29.096
-What…
-What?!

47:29.179 --> 47:30.848
Honey, I gotta go.

47:34.226 --> 47:35.519
Did he just

47:36.228 --> 47:37.229
hang up on me?

48:00.294 --> 48:01.795
What's happening?

48:01.879 --> 48:03.672
I need to get out! Let me out!

48:07.634 --> 48:08.468
What is this?

48:14.558 --> 48:15.642
No way, right?

48:15.726 --> 48:17.352
Lady Trainwreck isn't…

48:17.853 --> 48:20.772
She isn't in there right now, is she?

49:27.130 --> 49:29.925
-That fool still dares to lie!
-Could we get more bracken?

49:30.008 --> 49:31.843
-Coming right up.
-You there!

49:32.594 --> 49:34.721
Twist the legs of the traitor who…

49:34.805 --> 49:36.890
-You scared me!
-That table wants more bracken.

49:36.974 --> 49:40.102
Can't you take it to them?
It's the final scene.

49:40.185 --> 49:42.062
Yes, just a moment.

49:43.981 --> 49:46.316
-Hey, they slipped up!
-Where?

49:46.400 --> 49:47.609
You missed it.

49:49.528 --> 49:52.781
Go on and behead me!

49:55.325 --> 49:58.245
LOCATION PROVIDED BY KOREAN FOLK VILLAGE

49:58.328 --> 50:00.038
-Hey, look right there!
-Where?

50:00.122 --> 50:01.832
Oh, I see it!

50:01.915 --> 50:05.085
I heard they shoot scenes live nowadays.
Looks like it's true.

50:05.168 --> 50:09.214
A hospital gown in the Joseon Dynasty?
Why, that's something.

50:09.297 --> 50:11.008
I bet someone's in big trouble.

50:11.758 --> 50:13.343
I'm the one who caught it.

50:22.352 --> 50:23.687
Oh, right.

50:29.359 --> 50:30.193
Hello.

50:30.902 --> 50:31.778
Honey.

50:33.071 --> 50:34.948
Yes, sure. I'm heading back right now.

50:35.907 --> 50:39.036
No, I had some business
to quickly attend to at City Hall.

50:40.203 --> 50:41.455
No, right now, I'm…

50:41.955 --> 50:43.457
I'm already on my way back.

50:43.957 --> 50:44.791
What?

50:45.375 --> 50:47.753
No, I swear. I'll be back soon.

50:48.295 --> 50:49.546
Why's this happening again?

50:49.629 --> 50:52.841
Stop trying to change the subject.
When will you be back?

50:52.924 --> 50:53.759
What?

50:54.426 --> 50:55.886
I…

50:56.720 --> 50:57.846
An hour?

51:00.265 --> 51:01.308
The thing is,

51:01.892 --> 51:04.644
I'm going as fast as I can,
but there's traffic--

51:09.316 --> 51:11.276
Fine, I was playing hooky. So what?

51:12.444 --> 51:14.571
You think all I have to do
is make deliveries?

51:15.072 --> 51:17.032
I have personal business too.

51:17.115 --> 51:18.158
Okay?

51:18.742 --> 51:21.912
The person I hate most in the world
might be in danger.

51:21.995 --> 51:24.998
So hang up, and don't wait for me.

51:25.082 --> 51:26.124
I'm busy!

51:54.778 --> 51:55.612
What is that?

52:43.952 --> 52:45.287
Number 3972.

52:47.122 --> 52:48.874
So you're looking for something too.

53:12.647 --> 53:14.608
Her power isn't resurrection?

53:15.984 --> 53:17.027
Could it be…

53:19.487 --> 53:21.740
Wow, this is insane.

53:22.824 --> 53:24.701
Now she's in international waters?

53:25.785 --> 53:27.621
It was teleportation?

53:33.752 --> 53:34.628
When did you board?

53:36.087 --> 53:37.631
Are you a police officer?

53:40.467 --> 53:43.386
What did that bitch see
to have such a dumb look on her face?

53:43.470 --> 53:45.180
Stop yapping.

53:45.263 --> 53:48.308
Let's not waste time
and just throw her overboard as fish food!

53:49.059 --> 53:49.893
Okay.

53:58.235 --> 54:00.362
Help me.

54:28.932 --> 54:31.268
Has Madam King arrived already?

54:56.626 --> 54:58.920
Long time no see, Director Choi.

55:05.427 --> 55:07.429
LIFETIME ACHIEVEMENT AWARD
CHOI YEONG-JUN

58:50.193 --> 58:55.198
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
